# Coding Standards

## Hard rules

- Strict TypeScript — **no `any`**
- Prefer explicit domain types from `types/`
- Server Components first; `"use client"` only when required
- SOLID + Clean Architecture boundaries
- Repository pattern for data access
- Feature-based modules under `frontend/features/<name>/`
- Atomic Design under `components/{atoms,molecules,organisms}`

## Placement

| Concern | Put it in |
|---|---|
| Page / route | `app/` |
| UI primitive | `components/` |
| Feature UI / domain UI | `frontend/features/` |
| Mock / seed data | `frontend/data/` |
| Business service | `backend/services/` |
| Persistence adapter | `backend/repositories/` |
| Shared util | `lib/` |
| Domain type | `types/` |
| Hook | `hooks/` |
| Global CSS / tokens | `styles/` |

## Code quality

- Small, focused diffs — no drive-by refactors
- No unused exports or dead code
- Named exports preferred for shared modules
- Fail closed on authz once Auth is wired
- Match existing naming and import alias style (`@/`)

## Do not

- Put SQL or service-role secrets in client components
- Embed business rules inside atoms
- Flatten enterprise folders without updating docs
